{"schema": 1, "provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.1-pro-high", "request_sha256": "0acd8fda2776add22428fc4af81de427f4e44aeb70c8882fddbd42a88c4891ef", "invocation_metadata": {"schema": 1, "image_id": "sha256:aa4eae810628bd2b78bd48ed3059c284a497bdc7c92d81daacdfe906a3bae3ae", "executable_path": "/usr/local/bin/agy", "executable_sha256": "a759ce7c7a235d9b6c281a25ead97cbbf2e92314a3ffd224e2f9144f3fae7a86", "known_configuration_path": "/home/stev/.gemini/settings.json", "known_configuration_sha256": null, "other_effective_configuration": "unknown; trusted launcher/profile boundary"}, "native_exit_code": 0, "usage_reported": {"input_tokens": 42150, "output_tokens": 23726, "thinking_tokens": 23363, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 65876}, "result": {"schema": 1, "verdict": "reject", "reason": "Implementation fails to recover safely from crashes during phase application and leaks untrusted inputs via command line arguments.", "findings": [{"file": "src/specorganon/software_controller.py", "priority": "high", "problem": "Crash recovery fails if a crash occurs after mutating the engine state (e.g., via run_manifest or review_phase) but before clearing the pending status. On resume, the controller strictly requires fingerprint(current) == pending['source_fingerprint'], which raises a ControllerError and permanently blocks the case.", "concrete fix": "Update resumption logic to verify if the exact post-mutation state was achieved (or wrap the operation and history append in a robust state guard) so it can safely clear the pending state and resume instead of permanently crashing."}, {"file": "scripts/controller_native_role.py", "priority": "high", "problem": "For the Gemini provider, the role adapter passes the untrusted prompt (containing codebase documents and up to 128KB of text) directly on the command line via the '--print' argument. This leaks untrusted contents to system process lists and risks exceeding Linux MAX_ARG_STRLEN limits.", "concrete fix": "Pass the prompt via standard input (stdin_bytes) for Gemini, just as is done for Codex, and adjust the 'agy' invocation to read its input from standard input instead of argv."}], "tests_executed": false}}
